6. ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
   considered_vertices=runners,gaps,endpoint owners,route labels,certificate atoms,sidecar columns,discharge modes,proof obligations
   chosen_vertices=packet/route/certificate/sidecar/discharge coordinates
   preserved_lrc_predicate=boundary/open status plus exact route/certificate/discharge legality
   destroyed_if_raw=exact scale, endpoint owner, topology, sidecar obligation, and terminal discharge atom
   challenged_assumption=the final proof should not be a scalar route order; it should be a median-center legality test on completed packet states

READING
  The proposed final proof interface can be made finite: encode each
  packet route as a legal sidecar-closed coordinate set.  Legal sidecars
  are unary Horn implications here, so three legal packet states have a
  unique coordinatewise median center.  If that center keeps only the typed
  discharge coordinate and drops the specific atom, the proof has found
  a scheduler center: refine by a separating sidecar or name residual debt.
